---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Pillars from '../components/Pillars.astro';
import Proof from '../components/Proof.astro';
import RootsTeaser from '../components/RootsTeaser.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Shree Krishnamurthi — engineering, product, urban farming" path="/">
  <Hero />

  <section class="intro">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="intro__grid">
        <p class="eyebrow">The short version</p>
        <div class="intro__body">
          <p>
            I have spent about twenty five years taking things from zero to one. I was part of the founding engineering team on a physical security platform that grew into an enterprise product and got acquired. I left tech to build a food brand from nothing and got it to profitability in a year. Now I sit across the table from CTOs and product leaders, work backwards from their hardest problem, and get working AI in front of their customers in weeks instead of quarters.
          </p>
          <p>
            What we build is rarely the point. The point is to start a company's AI program, or to speed up one that has stalled, and to leave their engineers able to carry it themselves. One of those builds went further than that and became a feature inside an AWS service.
          </p>
          <p>
            I also helped start a community garden in Mountain View, where we teach people to grow their own food.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Pillars />
  <Proof />
  <RootsTeaser />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  .intro__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 10rem 1fr;
    column-gap: var(--space-6);
  }
  .intro__body {
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
  .intro__body p {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .intro__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; row-gap: var(--space-3); }
  }
</style>
